# Follow-up to 2026-09-25-33.play, same cell (mode=battleground map=flags
# spec=druid:feral view=1280x800 save=carried), style forced to `good`
# instead of `auto` for this probe.
#
# 33.play's `me` hud entry read hp=0/alive=false for the entire back half of
# the script -- 14s+ after the death that ended the first play() chunk, well
# past src/sim/battleground.ts's own RESPAWN_EARLY=6/RESPAWN_LATE=11, while
# the party's own alive count recovered in the same window (3/5 -> 4/5). That
# could be a real hud/respawn bug on the player's own slot specifically, or it
# could be the driver's own play()-aborts-on-hero-null quirk (already a known
# driver lesson) simply resampling too early each time. `state` alone never
# aborts on a null hero the way `play` does, so polling it directly, without
# a `play` call in between, is the only way to watch a respawn (or the lack
# of one) happen without the driver's own abort cutting the observation off.
open
tap battleground
tap map:flags
tap class:druid:feral
tap pull
waitscreen fight 15
play good 25
state
wait 5
state
wait 5
state
wait 5
state
wait 5
state
wait 5
state
shot after-probe
